note: Lists and maps: adding, changing and removing, slicing, nested values, and sharing.

set list inventory to ["sword", "shield"]
add "potion" to inventory
change inventory[1] to "magic staff"
print(inventory)
remove 2 from inventory
print(inventory)
remove "potion" from inventory
print(inventory)

set map profile to {"name": "Bob"}
change profile["level"] to 50
print(profile)
remove "level" from profile
print(profile)

note: change, add and remove work on anything that holds a value, however deep.
set list grid to [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
add 5 to grid[1]
change grid[2][1] to 30
print(grid)
set map team to {"scores": [10, 20]}
add 30 to team["scores"]
print(team)

note: Slices take both ends; negative positions count from the end.
set list nums to [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]
print(nums[2~4], nums[-1], nums[-3~-1])
set str greeting to "Hello World"
print(greeting[1~5], greeting[-5~-1])

note: Lists, maps and objects are shared, not copied. copy makes a separate list, one level deep.
set list a to [1, 2, 3]
set list b to a
add 4 to b
print(a)
set list c to copy(a)
add 5 to c
print(a, c)

note: A position that does not exist is an error, which or_else can catch.
set number safe_value to nums[99] or_else do:
    print("position 99 does not exist; using 0")
    change safe_value to 0
end
print(f"safe_value = {safe_value}")
